    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d923">

                <pb facs="0824" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/508a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-16T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>328. For Berlin. Norwegian steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Storstad</hi> under
                    charter to Commission for Relief in Belgium carrying 10,000 tons corn from <pb
                        facs="0825" n="653" xml:id="pg653"/> Buenos Aires to Rotterdam, was sunk
                    without warning by German submarine off coast of Ireland, March 7 or 8. German
                    Government will, of course, recognize that sinking of commission’s ships in
                    violation of understanding strikes at the root of relief work in Belgium and
                    northern France. This Government can not encourage commission to continue its
                    work unless it has most positive assurances that no more of its ships will be
                    sunk.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
